oblem and i  don't think deshawn watson's the kind of  guy who plays around he's not trying  some leverage deal i think once you lose  him you've lost him there's no getting  him back that's just my hunch gut  feeling based on knowing him talking to  him being around him i don't know him  all that well but i don't think he's  going to be a guy who plays games you  know he's not going to be into the drama  like oh i don't know ben roethlisberger  would be he's going to say he wants out  or suggest he wants out or think he  wants out only if wait for it he wants  out  yeah i'm  right there with you mike i i do think  he might be at that point where there's  no turning back and the bur the bridge  has been burned down and  he maybe the best option for him is this  at this point is going elsewhere and if  he pushes that i mean the texas can say  all they want we're not trading you but  if deshawn watson wants out he can make  it where the texans have to trade him  because he is just as you said an  employee you show up only when you have  to show up you do the bare minimum and  eventually they're going to get rid of  you and we're seeing it in the nba in  the same city with james harden mike  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

